wer in radians. Using a calculator in \"radians\" mode, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0.8)=0.674\\,740…≈0.675\\,\\text{radians}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073681 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3a2e44aa-d511-5bb4-bfe3-3213d7df0f1a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Trigonometric Ratio of an Acute Special Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "137571b5-7a83-5f63-8a0b-fcf213a92f6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545235} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff39d9b-b653-56bf-aa12-7a8401ca193a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545348} {:answer/id #uuid "b258fa98-837b-58ac-bb50-87dbe84ce48b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545521} {:answer/id #uuid "b4f2c0d5-f400-5694-82c6-4b8a8fb68adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545529} {:answer/id #uuid "da283058-2c21-59b1-a080-2b672e4fb121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4f2c0d5-f400-5694-82c6-4b8a8fb68adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545529} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6f86bd3-1e4e-5923-9c4e-69ac157875db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f375dc2-c494-589d-83fe-86d9688ddf86" :question/math-academy-id "q-54386" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ radians to an equivalent measure in degrees. This gives\n\n$$\n(\\frac{\\pi }{6})(\\frac{{180}^{∘}}{\\pi })=\\frac{{180}^{∘}}{6}={30}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since we know that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545858 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073681 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3a2e44aa-d511-5bb4-bfe3-3213d7df0f1a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Trigonometric Ratio of an Acute Special Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a11dbc5-4605-5d2f-815d-487cdff0ae65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545252} {:answer/id #uuid "4a933bd3-9d4d-5635-b3d2-b0ca7cff973e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545341} {:answer/id #uuid "b56b841a-b4a3-56c7-bfa1-a682e8e14500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545530} {:answer/id #uuid "bb5dd636-0a57-50f3-a3b6-1ac51a1c9db9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545538} {:answer/id #uuid "bd197a7f-2045-5bf2-9e98-404a33fb8ace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb5dd636-0a57-50f3-a3b6-1ac51a1c9db9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545538} :answer-field/id #uuid "27912ff0-a6bc-5a3b-9141-25760180fb99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c68e45a3-bbd1-5372-b99a-a88344f8278f" :question/math-academy-id "q-54387" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ radians to an equivalent measure in degrees. This gives\n\n$$\n(\\frac{\\pi }{3})(\\frac{{180}^{∘}}{\\pi })=\\frac{{180}^{∘}}{3}={60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\operatorname{tan}⁡{60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since we know that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\sqrt{3},$  we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\operatorname{tan}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$"}]}
